## Implementation summary

### Worker state

`llama_worker/state/workerState.mjs` now owns:

- static worker model path resolution from `import.meta.url` and base config;
- initialization of worker-local mutable slots:
  - `model`;
  - `ready`;
  - `initPromise`;
  - `resetting`;
  - `shuttingDown`;
  - `activeConfig`;
  - `activeInitAttemptId`;
  - `activeProfileName`;
  - `nextActiveRequestSequence`;
  - `sessions`;
  - `activeRequests`;
  - `workerOperationChain`.

`llama_worker/llama.mjs` creates one `workerState` object and rewires existing reads/writes to that object.

The model path remains derived from the base config at worker startup. It is still passed to `loadModel()` as `workerState.modelPath`; it is not derived from mutable `activeConfig` or `configSnapshot`.

### Worker operation queue

`llama_worker/serialization/workerOperationQueue.mjs` now owns the `workerOperationChain` mutation through `createWorkerOperationQueue(state)`.

The queue logic remains mechanically equivalent:

```js
const run = state.workerOperationChain.then(fn, fn);
state.workerOperationChain = run.catch(() => {});
return run;
```

No lifecycle serialization behavior was changed.

### Prompt abort error

`llama_worker/errors/promptAbort.mjs` now owns `createPromptAbortError(message, meta = {})`.

The helper preserves:

- `err.name = "PromptAbortError"`;
- `err.isPromptAbort = true`;
- assignment of metadata fields onto the error object.

### Outbound messages

`llama_worker/messages/outboundMessages.mjs` now owns worker-to-parent message construction through `createOutboundMessages(parentPort)`.

It provides helpers for:

- `ready`;
- `stream`;
- `done`;
- `reset_done`;
- `model_reset_done`;
- `shutdown_done`;
- `error`.

The helper preserves the existing protocol shape and keeps `llama_worker/llama.mjs` responsible for dispatch/routing decisions.

## Propagation review

- `tests/helpers/runtimeFixtureFiles.mjs` was updated to include the four new worker modules.
- Active smoke tests with local `RUNTIME_FILES` arrays were updated to match the shared manifest.
- `tests/legacy/smokeTestModelResetIdleIsolation.mjs` was not modified because it is legacy/reference material and is excluded by the active fixture coverage guard.
- `workerBridge.mjs` still targets `./llama_worker/llama.mjs`.
- No module under `llama_worker/**` imports `llama_worker/llama.mjs` or `workerBridge.mjs`.
- No root `inference.mjs` was introduced.

