## Real-runtime testing

Not run in this sandbox.

This branch touches worker state, worker operation serialization storage, prompt abort error construction, and prompt streaming message construction. Michael-side real-runtime testing is recommended before merge readiness unless explicitly waived.

Recommended real-runtime gates:

```bash
REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestWorkerNativeCancellationBoundary.mjs
REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestContextCreationCancelBoundary.mjs
REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestWorkerOperationSerialization.mjs
REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestDrainShutdown.mjs
node ./tests/smokeTestInitThenResetWithoutPriorPrompt.mjs
node ./tests/smokeTestLifecycleRegression.mjs
```

## Caveats / known risks

- Sandbox/mock tests do not prove native/model behavior.
- This branch intentionally rewires the worker's top-level mutable slots through a state object. The preflight tests passed, but real-runtime validation should still cover prompt streaming, cancellation, context creation, reset, and shutdown behavior.
- The existing known intermittent real-runtime timeout caveat around lifecycle retry/reset/shutdown remains a carry-forward caveat; this branch does not address native resource timing.

## Recommended next branch after acceptance

```text
worker-layout-option-c-disposal-primitives-v1
```

Suggested scope for the next branch:

```text
llama_worker/session/sessionDisposal.mjs
llama_worker/context/contextOptions.mjs
llama_worker/prompt/chunkFactory.mjs
minimal llama_worker/llama.mjs rewiring only
```

Keep cancellation, context retry service, session service, lifecycle services, prompt runner, and router extraction out of that next branch unless the plan/spec is explicitly revised.
